Coming next Releases
Value Drop 3 is focused on MCP integration and tooling, MCP observability and Human Feedback enablement.
The following capabilities are part of Value Drops4 & 5:
•	Agent-to-Agent (A2A) collaboration.
•	AGUI integration.
•	Durable Agents.
•	Agentic Evaluation & Testing beyond the Human Evaluation capability described above.
•	Long-Term Memory.
•	Rolling out identity/security capabilities.
•	Enhanced DevSecOps and Offensive Security target-state capabilities.
•	Strategic AI Gateway target state.
A2A and AGUI are later platform capabilities and should not be inferred from Release 3's MCP support. MCP in VD3 provides governed agent-to-tool/service integration; it does not constitute delivery of the later agent-to-agent collaboration capability. The current program baseline places A2A and AGUI in Release 5.
The strategic AI Gateway is also not a VD3 capability. APIM V1 remains the current AIPT2 program architecture, while the strategic AI Gateway target state is proposed for consideration through Architecture Reset.
